cxi_user: add force_avoid_wc parameter (test only)

Test patch, not a proposed fix. Lets the existing arm64 avoid_writecombine
path in ucxi_mmap() (pgprot_device instead of pgprot_writecombine for CQ
launch pages) be enabled at runtime on platforms other than Ampere Altra:

  echo 1 > /sys/module/cxi_user/parameters/force_avoid_wc

It is evaluated at mmap time, so it applies to command queues allocated
after the write. Kernel command queues (ioremap_wc in cass_cq.c) are not
affected.

Against shs-cxi-driver release/shs-13.1.0 (built and tested). Also applies
cleanly to release/shs-14.0.1 (not built or tested there).

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/hpe/ss1/cxi_user_mmap.c	2026-11-03 23:38:52
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/hpe/ss1/cxi_user_mmap.c	2026-11-03 23:39:04
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@
 #include <linux/fs.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
+
 #include "cxi_prov_hw.h"
 #include "cxi_user.h"
 
@@ -39,6 +41,18 @@
 	.close = cxi_vma_close,
 };
 
+/* cxi_xlat harness test patch (not upstream): map CQ launch pages as Device
+ * memory instead of write-combined (arm64 Normal-NC). Normal-NC mappings allow
+ * speculative CPU reads, which hit the launch pages as 64-byte MRd TLPs and are
+ * logged as C_PI_EXT pri_mb_xlat_pf_addr_error + pri_mb_xlat_comp_ca on Grace.
+ * Checked at mmap time, so it can be toggled at runtime via
+ * /sys/module/cxi_user/parameters/force_avoid_wc for new command queues.
+ */
+static bool force_avoid_wc;
+module_param(force_avoid_wc, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(force_avoid_wc,
+		 "Map CQ launch pages as device memory instead of write-combined (test)");
+
 /* This is a copy of vm_iomap_memory() with a small change. It appears
  * that vm_iomap_memory only works when the physical page are mapped
  * from the first page of the mapping. If we map something else before
@@ -124,7 +138,8 @@
 	case MMAP_PHYSICAL:
 		if (ip->wc)
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM64
-			if (static_branch_unlikely(&avoid_writecombine)) {
+			if (static_branch_unlikely(&avoid_writecombine) ||
+			    READ_ONCE(force_avoid_wc)) {
 				vma->vm_page_prot =
 					pgprot_device(vma->vm_page_prot);
 				pr_warn("Broken PCIe write-combine detected on this platform, LL_RING will use slow workaround and should be avoided in userspace.");
